----------------------------------------------------------------------
2. FULL PROBLEM vs the frozen reference (20,000 particles per solve)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Reference: reference/lattice_x*.npz (mc.py, 40,000,000 histories at scale 1),
checked against OpenMC.  Error = mean over 6 GMC solves of the relative
L2 difference of the 7x7 cell fluxes.  Floor = the same number for
6 independent mc.py solves at the same particle count, i.e.
what an exact method scores.  Ratio 1.00 = as good as Monte Carlo.
Bias = the 6 GMC fields averaged; "noise only" is what that
average would score if the model were exact.  cell chi2: per-cell bias
test over the cells one 20,000-particle MC solve resolves to better than
20% (count in brackets), in units of the model runs' own spread.
Exact Monte Carlo scores 0.3-2.3 (mean ~1); well above ~2.5 = systematic error.

